  h1 Emergency Water Damage &amp; Flood Restoration in Sydney

  p.service-page__lede When water is spreading through your home right now — a burst flexi-hose under the sink, a washing-machine hose that's let go, storm water through the roof, or flooding through the ground floor — it's an emergency, and the clock starts the moment it happens. drySafe handles emergency water damage restoration across Sydney, fully self-serve — you book and pay online, with no callback or quote to arrange first.

  p Water damage is rarely as contained as it looks. Within the first hours it soaks down through carpet into the underlay, wicks up the base of plasterboard walls, and tracks along the subfloor and into timber framing — well beyond the wet patch you can actually see. That hidden spread is what turns a manageable spill into warped boards, lifting skirting, odour and lasting structural repair. It's also why what happens in the first day counts for more than almost anything that comes later.

  a.btn-primary(href='https://drysafe.vercel.app/get-started?utm_source=website') Book &amp; pay online

  section.service-page__process
    h2 What happens on an emergency job
    p Restoration done properly is a sequence, not a mop and a fan pointed at the damp. On a drySafe job it runs in order, and each step earns the next:
    ul
      li #[strong Assessment] — we map how far the water has actually travelled using moisture readings, and check the water category, so the plan matches the real spread rather than the surface.
      li #[strong Extraction] — the standing and absorbed water is drawn out of carpet, underlay and hard floors before drying starts, because you can't dry a room that's still holding water.
      li #[strong Drying] — high-velocity air movers push air across the wet materials while a dehumidifier pulls the released moisture out of the room, so the structure itself dries rather than just the surface skinning over.
      li #[strong Verified dry] — readings taken against the IICRC S500 dry standard confirm the home is genuinely back to normal, and the result is documented for your own records and your insurer.

  section.service-page__area
    h2 Across Greater Sydney
    p drySafe works throughout Greater Sydney — the City of Parramatta, Cumberland, Ryde and The Hills among the council areas covered. Booking is built to be simple: booked and paid for online, with no callback to arrange.

  section.service-page__packages
    h2 What's included
    p Two levels, so the response scales to how deep the water went:
    ul
      li #[strong drySafe Basic] covers the emergency essentials: high-velocity air movers and a surface moisture assessment — enough to begin drying the affected materials and to see where the water has reached.
      li #[strong drySafe Care] adds dehumidification and full moisture analytics, tracking the dry-down through to a verified, documented result. It's the option when water has gone deep or reached materials that hold moisture and need measuring over days, not hours.

  section.service-page__pricing
    h2 What it costs
    p A traditional water-damage response usually starts with a paid call-out — around #[strong $499] for someone to attend and quote before any work happens. drySafe replaces that step with a fixed online price: book and pay online from #[strong $302], with no assessment fee. Booking online instead of paying for a traditional call-out saves you nearly 40%.
    p.service-page__disclaimer *From-prices are per room and exclude GST, any after-hours surcharge and package upgrades. After-hours surcharges are calculated at the time of booking based on drySafe's business-hours schedule.

  a.btn-primary(href='https://drysafe.vercel.app/get-started?utm_source=website') Book &amp; pay online

